+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` already exists in `src/index.ts` with helpers (`isObject`, `deepEqual`, pointer parsing). `createPatch` is its inverse.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** correct (round-trips through `applyPatch`) and small patches; no mutation.
+**Non-Goals:** guaranteeing the globally shortest patch; emitting `copy` or `test`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Recursive diff.** Equal values give nothing; two objects diff per key (removes, then recursive diffs of common keys, then adds); two arrays diff by alignment; anything else is a `replace` at that path (root included, path `""`).
+- **Arrays via LCS.** Common prefix/suffix are trimmed, then a longest common subsequence over `deepEqual` aligns items. Items between matches are a gap of removed and added items: the first min(removed, added) are paired and diffed recursively in place, leftovers become `remove` or `add`. A running index tracks the position in the partially patched array, so paths are valid when applied sequentially. Items outside gaps are never touched.
+- **Moves as remove + add.** An item moved elsewhere appears as one removal and one addition, which the spec permits; emitting `move` is not needed.
+- **Cloning.** Values placed in the patch are `structuredClone`d.
+- Pointer tokens are escaped (`~`→`~0`, `/`→`~1`). Own enumerable keys only (`Object.keys`/`Object.hasOwn`), safe for `__proto__`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- LCS is O(n·m) on the trimmed middle; acceptable for typical payloads.
