+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document instead of the whole new version. The library can apply RFC 6902 patches but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when applied with `applyPatch`.
+- The patch is minimal in size in spirit: it descends into objects and arrays and describes only the differing places; it never resends the whole document for a small change.
+- Array insertions and removals yield a single `add`/`remove`; moved items yield `move` or `remove` + `add`, without rewriting items in between.
+- Neither input is mutated, and the patch shares no structure with them.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-diff`: producing an RFC 6902 JSON Patch from two JSON documents.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new exported function; `src/index.test.ts`: new tests.
+- No new dependencies, no change to existing behavior.
